** Purpose
Provides an Emacs front-end for fzf, a general purpose fuzzy finder.
Supports fuzzy searching files, buffers, git files, grep, and more
in a terminal popup. Note: =M-x fzf= uses =FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND= and
is not for opening files — use =fzf-find-file= for that.

** Commands
| Command                       | Description                        |
|-------------------------------+------------------------------------|
| =fzf=                         | Run fzf using FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND  |
| =fzf-find-file=               | Fuzzy find and open a file         |
| =fzf-find-file-in-dir=        | Fuzzy find in a specific directory |
| =fzf-recentf=                 | Fuzzy search recent files          |
| =fzf-git-files=               | Fuzzy search git-tracked files     |
| =fzf-git-grep=                | Fuzzy grep in git repo             |
| =fzf-switch-buffer=           | Fuzzy switch buffer                |
| =fzf-grep=                    | Fuzzy grep                         |

